 {"id": "README-11", "title": "P4 — README.md:415 and :443 promise semantic ?q= 'fails closed' with 503 EMBEDDINGS_UNAVAILABLE when embeddings are down, but at HEAD it silently degrades to the keyword leg and returns 200 with scored results, so an operator cannot tell semantic search is dead", "priority": "P4", "status": "pending", "created_by": null, "created_at": "2026-10-19T20:03:10Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-19T20:24:25Z", "reasoning": "Truth check 2026-10-19 against a live daemon on a fresh clone (port 3779, DUCKBRAIN_EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=openai with no API key at HEAD 42fbc88d). The README claims (README.md:415, repeated at :443) that with embeddings down the endpoint fails closed with an explicit message and that on a current build this is 503 EMBEDDINGS_UNAVAILABLE, never a silent result. MEASURED: /health -> HTTP 503 with embedding.healthy=false, note 'missing API key (DUCKBRAIN_EMBEDDING_API_KEY)' (so the daemon agrees embeddings are down), yet GET /api/memories?namespace=quickstart&q=quickstart -> HTTP 200 with the memory and score 0.1718 — below the 0.25 semantic floor the same README documents — and no warning field in the body; the only signal is the server log line '[recall] Embedding failed on openai/..., trying next provider: ... embed HTTP 401'. A namespace with no FTS sidecar answers the same way: HTTP 200 with an empty item list, still not 503. Code path: src/mcp/tools/recall.ts:1166-1197 is a keyword-only offline fallback that returns keyword results whenever the FTS sidecar works and only surfaces the semantic error when BOTH legs are unavailable; src/http/routes/memories.ts:53-77 maps that error to 503 EMBEDDINGS_UNAVAILABLE. The fallback landed with the hybrid search work (RETR-002, c1ddfca9 2026-08-18), i.e. before this README text was last touched. FIX: say plainly that ?q= is hybrid (semantic + keyword, RETR-002) and that when no provider can embed the request is served from the keyword leg (keyword scores, 200, no semantic ranking), reserving the 503 sentence for the case where the keyword leg is unavailable too; if the product wants a visible signal for degraded semantic search that is an owner decision and a separate row, not this one. Doc severity P4 by ruling 2026-09-30. ch:trace row=README-11 spec=README.md#L412-415 doc=README.md evidence=live:http://127.0.0.1:3779/health=503 with embedding healthy=false, plus GET /api/memories?namespace=quickstart&q=quickstart -> 200 score=0.1718 witness=live:http://127.0.0.1:3779/api/memories?namespace=quickstart&q=quickstart verdict=none:doc row pending commit=none:not-yet-fixed memory=none:lane-local finding", "capability_tags": [], "complexity": 2, "detail": {"fingerprint": "38394ad3a8dfba1c8f81918388d520cfd0c2e61d1791b5bd3c25c0472ba233b0"}, "foreman_note": "Re-verified at HEAD 42fbc88d this tick (duckbrain-readme lane, second pass) — premise HOLDS, with a sharper measurement than the original row: with NO provider able to embed (daemon started DUCKBRAIN_EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=openai DUCKBRAIN_EMBEDDING_API_KEY=invalid-probe DUCKBRAIN_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9/v1), /health reports embedding {healthy:false, provider:\"\", providers:[{id:openai,healthy:false,note:\"fetch failed\"}]} while GET /api/memories?namespace=quickstart&q=connection+pooling answers http_code=200 in 0.074s with {\"items\":[],\"total\":0,\"count\":0} — i.e. not the documented 503 EMBEDDINGS_UNAVAILABLE and not even a keyword-leg fallback: a silent empty SUCCESS. Acceptance test for the fix therefore has two layers: (a) ?q= with no usable provider must answer 503 EMBEDDINGS_UNAVAILABLE (README.md:415,443), (b) it must never answer 200 with a zero-result body that reads as 'no matches'. Fresh evidence: /home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/readme/duckbrain/evidence/2026-10-19-http-surface.txt section B. Doc-severity unchanged (P4); this note is new measurement, not a re-triage.", "depends_on": []}
